# netsurf: getComputedStyle answers border-radius, gaps, box-shadow,
# tab-size and aspect-ratio (patch 295)
# Generated 2026-10-14
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 294)
#
# The native getComputedStyle (macsurf_qjs.c) answered only the
# properties on its list; border-radius, row-gap, column-gap, gap,
# box-shadow, tab-size and aspect-ratio were never among them, so
# the polyfill's wrapper filled them from its initial-value table --
# or, for border-radius and tab-size, with '' -- whatever the style
# sheet said. Code that lays out from computed values (measured
# toolbars, gap-aware canvas drawing, shadow-aware hit areas) read
# the initial values of a page that visibly had others.
#
# The native now answers all seven from the same computed style it
# already reads, in the reference serialization: a single radius as
# "12px" (a percentage stays "50%" -- the cascade cannot resolve
# it); the gaps per axis, with gap composed row-then-column and
# "normal" when unset; box-shadow as the colour-first list
# ("rgb(10, 20, 30) 2px 3px 4px 5px", inset last, shadows in
# order, "none" when there are none), from libcss's full shadow
# list, a currentColor shadow taking the element's colour; tab-size
# as its number (libcss's accessor already defaults it to 8);
# aspect-ratio reduced ("16 / 9" -- the parser stores thousandths,
# 16000 / 9000, so a fractional ratio survives) and "auto" when
# unset. Because the values are set inside the same if (style)
# block as the rest, the no-box cascade path (patch 235) answers
# them too. Two small helpers carry the formatting: qjs_cs_len_str
# (a length or percentage) and qjs_cs_colour_str (qjs_cs_colour's
# formatting into a buffer, for colours composed into a list).
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/CSS-gcs-props.html (GCSPROPS 9/9 in the
# simulator and in a reference browser -- Firefox/Camoufox, for the
# reason patch 292's header gives -- with identical strings). The
# values come from a style sheet, not inline style, on purpose: the
# wrapper answers an inline value when the native one is missing,
# which would mask the miss; and the checks run after load, when
# the elements have boxes, since at parse time this engine's
# computed style has no cascade to answer from yet (colour
# included). Simulator only; the vita cross-build was not run (no
# vitaSDK on this VM). Device expectation is in Doc 10.
#
# Decline conditions: none expected -- this is the native's own
# property list growing, in place.
#
